  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your soul has become entwined with your Awakened Spellbook. While the book is on your person, you have Advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks.</p><p>Moreover, if you take damage while your spellbook's mind is manifested, you can take a Reaction to prevent all of that damage by dismissing the spectral mind and using its magic to save yourself. Then roll 3d6: the spellbook temporarily loses spells of your choice whose combined spell level equals that roll or higher. If there aren't enough spells in the book to cover this cost, you drop to 0 Hit Points. Until you finish 1d6 Long Rests, you can't cast the lost spells, even from a scroll or another spellbook; after that, they reappear in the spellbook. Once you take this Reaction, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
